      "writtenOn": "2020-07-16T03:44:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this mean we allow 2 rt tasks on this cpu? At the moment, there is one rt task sync waking up another rt task, which is not enqueued yet, so there could be another unrelated rt task on this cpu. After the sync callee is enqueued (the caller should be sleeping now), it has to compare its prio with that unrelated rt task. I\u0027m not sure if it is intended design, just want to share that in CFS, we check that \"cpu_rq(cpu)-\u003enr_running \u003d\u003d 1\" to make sure the callee could run immediately.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1371,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1371,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "27c92e8f4e10bdc7e25b5616ca750b349e81cd68",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "639a8436_17fffba8",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/rt.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 1371,
      "author": {
        "id": 1456182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-20T16:26:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "should_honor_rt_sync() is called from select_task_rq_rt() and enqueue_task_rt(). In the former, checking for \u003d\u003d 1 could be useful because p is not enqueued yet. In the latter, the condition above is correct because now rt_nr_running takes into account the woken up RT task.\n\nIt depends on the intended use case, the current implementation could select this_cpu but then at enqueue find out that there are more than 2 RT task and add it to pushable tasks list. If we do check for \u003d\u003d 1 in select_task_rq_rt(), then we try to push the new task faster. But in both cases I\u0027d expect a push to be triggered.\n\nFrom my observation profiling RT tasks in Android, having a clash is quite rare. So the current implementation looks correct to me.",
      "parentUuid": "37ff6e45_01c138df",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1371,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 1371,
        "endChar": 27
